menu "PIV smart-card token"

config WOZ_PIV_CCID
	bool "Expose a native-USB PIV/CCID token (VM bench only)"
	depends on IDF_TARGET_ESP32S3
	default n
	help
	  Enumerate the ESP32-S3 native USB-OTG port as a single-slot CCID
	  smart-card reader containing a PIV application.

	  Keep this OFF for ordinary firmware development. A host Mac can claim a
	  PIV device during enumeration and offer to pair it with a local account.
	  Enable it only for tightly controlled validation in the disposable
	  Parallels macOS guest, with the board's separate USB-UART connection kept
	  available for flashing and recovery.

	  This initial option does not alter LoginWindow or enforce smart-card
	  authentication. Account pairing remains a separate, explicit VM step.

config WOZ_PIV_UWB_ONLY
	bool "Permit private-key operations without a PIV PIN (custom CTK lab only)"
	depends on WOZ_PIV_CCID
	default n
	help
	  Permit GENERAL AUTHENTICATE without a preceding PIV VERIFY command.
	  Slot 9A still signs only after the Aliro reader completes a fresh trusted
	  Wallet/UWB proof. Slot 9D key agreement is available without a PIN so
	  macOS can unwrap the login keychain.

	  Keep this OFF with Apple's built-in PIV token driver, which presents and
	  enforces its own PIN workflow. Enable it only in a disposable macOS VM
	  using OpenAliro's custom CryptoTokenKit extension, with password fallback
	  and a rescue administrator retained.

endmenu
